WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.596
The same sentence, said by a different person —

00:00:03.566 --> 00:00:06.951
or heard on a different day — is a DIFFERENT SENTENCE.

00:00:06.921 --> 00:00:12.370
What lands as a whisper from a peer can land as a SIREN from a manager.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.577
We are taught that communication is about choosing the right words.

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:19.236
I spent years polishing the words.

00:00:19.206 --> 00:00:22.144
Turns out, the words are only HALF of it.

00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:23.624
I once told the team:

00:00:23.594 --> 00:00:26.036
"We need to tighten our project timeline."

00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:29.856
One engineer heard: small adjustments.

00:00:29.826 --> 00:00:32.188
Another heard: DROP EVERYTHING.

00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:34.234
Same words. Same meeting.

00:00:34.204 --> 00:00:37.133
And here's the part I learned the hard way.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:41.413
At a final perf review — with genuinely good results —

00:00:41.383 --> 00:00:45.133
I asked one question, out of pure curiosity:

00:00:45.103 --> 00:00:48.529
"Why is this number different from what we expected?"

00:00:48.499 --> 00:00:53.209
Over the next few days, team members found me, one by one,

00:00:53.179 --> 00:00:56.299
quietly asking what my REAL concern was.

00:00:56.269 --> 00:00:59.679
Whether I thought the project had FAILED.

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:02.073
I didn't. I was just curious.

00:01:02.043 --> 00:01:05.289
But it was the performance review season.

00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:08.819
Everyone's sensitivity was turned all the way UP.

00:01:08.789 --> 00:01:14.059
And my title meant my question left my mouth at VOLUME 3 —

00:01:14.029 --> 00:01:16.043
and arrived at VOLUME 10.

00:01:16.013 --> 00:01:20.033
That's the thing about titles: when your title changes,

00:01:20.003 --> 00:01:21.856
your default volume changes with it.

00:01:21.826 --> 00:01:26.880
A comment that used to be one opinion becomes THE DIRECTION.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.521
You don't get to opt out of this.

00:01:29.491 --> 00:01:32.241
So here is my working theory:

00:01:32.211 --> 00:01:37.241
leadership communication is like adjusting a speaker's volume.

00:01:37.211 --> 00:01:39.741
The message isn't just the words —

00:01:39.711 --> 00:01:42.900
it's the words, times WHO YOU ARE, times WHERE THEY ARE.
